  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Justice and Legal Empowerment in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project aims to meaningfully expand access to justice and institutionalize inclusive legal empowerment mechanisms across Egypt, with focus particular on vulnerable and marginalized populations, including women, refugees, and underserved communities. Firmly grounded in Egypt&#x2019;s Vision 2030, the Government Work Programme (2024&#x2013;2027), and SDG 16 on Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions, the initiative responds to emerging national priorities, most notably, the enactment of Asylum Law No. 164 of 2024. This legislation introduces a new legal framework for refugees in Egypt.</narrative>
  </description>
